<title>USA: Frequency clarifies dividend policy.</title>
<headline>Frequency clarifies dividend policy.</headline>
<dateline>MITCHEL FIELD, N.Y. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Frequency Electronics Inc said Friday that its new policy of setting annual dividends at roughly 25 percent of the previous year's earnings is only a guideline, not a precise indication of what its earnings will be.</p>
<p>The company which expects to pay $0.30 in annual dividends this year, emphasized that it does not neccessarily expect annual earnings of $1.20 per share.</p>
<p>Earnings through the company's third fiscal quarter, ended Jan 31, totaled $0.72 a share.</p>
<p>The company said it has issued a clarification of its dividend policy in response to inquiries by securities analysts.</p>
</text>
